\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. There is a book, who runs may read,
\par Which heavenly truth imparts, 
\par And all the lore its scholars need,
\par Pure eyes and Christian hearts.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The works of god above, below,
\par Within us and around, 
\par Are pages in that book, to show
\par How God Himself is found.
\par  
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The glorious sky, embracing all, 
\par Is like the maker's love,
\par Wherewith encompassed, great and small
\par In peace and order move.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. One Name above all glorious names, 
\par With its ten thousand tongues 
\par The everlasting sea proclaims, 
\par Echoing angelic songs. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Two worlds are ours: 'tis only sin 
\par Forbids us to descry   \tab 
\par The mystic heaven and earth within, 
\par Plain as the sea and sky.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Thou, who hast given me eyes to see
\par And love this sight so fair, 
\par Give me a heart to find out Thee, 
\par And read Thee everywhere. 
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

